00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:29.730
And we have garam masala,
adding mint and parsley,

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.010
and I'm gonna add salt.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.013
This, it's gonna be flavor explosion.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.040
It's spicy but it's good spicy.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.270
Little bit more salt.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.330
Sometimes when I eat too spicy food

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.820
I feel like my ears are gonna fall off,

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.170
but this one doesn't have that.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.090
The bread is still a little bit dry,

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.400
so I want to put it in a refrigerator

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.160
so everything gonna soak
up all the goodness.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:56.970
So I'm going to cover this
and I'm going to rest this

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.460
in the refrigerator about 30 minutes.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.440
So this step I will need
my little surgery gloves.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.270
Leg of lamb.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.800
And another Tasty hack,

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.490
if you don't have dedicated
cutting board for meat

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.560
you can just wrap with plastic,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.750
so it doesn't cross-contaminate.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.170
You want to use flat part of meat pounder

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.500
and you want to pound
meat and kind of smear.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.450
The reason you want to pound
meat is to tenderize the meat

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.570
and also you want to
make it even thickness.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.010
It's gonna take a little time

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:35.370
and I'm gonna pound this
a little more flatter,

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.704
but before that, let's get fancy.

00:04:37.704 --> 00:04:40.121
(soft piano)

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:57.467
(upbeat rock music)

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.980
All right, I finish pounding
the meat and trimmed the meat

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.810
because it was a little too big.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.400
Now, I'm going to stuff this lamb.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.400
I'm going to put here and
I'm going to roll this over.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.450
This part is a little
thin, so I'm going to trim

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.480
just because I want to
make sure it cook evenly.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.090
We are going to cook this together

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.660
and I'm going to score just a little bit,

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.260
