of get into the meat.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.260
It's like diagonal and just
season surface of the meat

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.250
with salt and pepper.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.010
And I'm going to use butcher twine.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.560
And make sure to use butcher twine

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.230
because if you use other kind of string,

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.910
it might burn in oven.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.460
You can find butcher
twine in a grocery store.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.130
And I'm going to tie this meat

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.440
because it's kind of rolled up,

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:55.590
and if you don't tie it,
it's gonna fall apart.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.210
Kind of make L shape.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.160
When you tie with butcher twine,

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:03.090
you don't wanna tie too tight
because while it's cooking

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:06.030
it's kind of like steam
and expand and shrink.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.030
Purpose of tying is just hold the shape.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.820
All right, and this is done,

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.820
and I'm going to cut extra string.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:18.450
Move it to sheet pan
with cooling rack on top.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.650
Beautiful.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.530
I'm going to bake this at 350 oven

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:26.400
